Name: trait-make
License File: LICENSE
Description: Utilities for working with impl traits in Rust

# What is this crate used for?

Trait variant generation for Rust traits.

# Are there any use restrictions? i.e. only for development hosts

No.

# What differs from upstream?

While the crate is licensed under Apache and MIT, as stated both in the crates's
development repository (https://github.com/fitzgen/trait-make) and on its package
on crates.io, the crates.io distribution does not ship both LICENSE files.
Thus, we vendor in the repsitory from GitHub.
This can be un-forked when a release including the following pull request has been
pushed to crates.io: https://github.com/Sherlock-Holo/impl-trait-utils/pull/1

# Are there any restrictions to how it should be rolled?

No.

# Is there anything else which makes this dependency "special"?

No.
